
ERROR LOGS found in the book
``Computer Organization and Design -- The Hardware/Software Interface''
John L. Hennessy & David A. Patterson
copyright 1994, first print.

Notations:
P. for page number.
| show printed in the book.
S: suggested correction.

P.66, next to last line
| e vencorrect
S:
  even correct

P.80, SPECINT and SPECFP is commonly spelled as
S:
  PSECint and SPECfp.

P.95, second set of MIPS intructions
|  add a, b, c    # ...   a. add a,
|  a, d           # ...   a. add a,
|  a, e           # ...   is now in a.
S:
  add a, b, c    # ...   a.
  add a, a, d    # ...   a.
  add a, a, e    # ...   is now in a.

P.112, 10th line from below
| "else" part. Weh i j, the
S:
  "else" part. Weh i!=j, the

P.114, mult instruction, mul is better
| mult $9, 
S:
  mul $9, ...

P.116,  Loop: unnecessary, also mult, and $19 should be $10
| Loop: mult $9, $19, $21 # Temporary reg $9 
S:
        mul $9, $10, $21 # Temporary reg $9 

P.118, Figure 3.11, MIPS machine language
| jr  R  0  31  0  0  0  8  jr $1
S:
  jr  R  0  31  0  0  0  8  jr $31

P.132, Figure 3.16, MIPS machine language
| jr  R  0  31  0  0  0  8  jr $1
S:
  jr  R  0  31  0  0  0  8  jr $31

P.141,  4 times j
| add $16, $4, $15  # reg 16 = v + j
S:
  add $16, $4, $15  # reg 16 = v + j*4

P.144,  4 times j
| Inner loop add $16, $4, $15  # reg 16 = v + j
S:
Inner loop   add $16, $4, $15  # reg 16 = v + j*4

P.177, Figure 4.3, ">" missing
|        A + B     0          0        <0
|        A + B    <0         <0         0
|        A - B     0         <0        <0
|        A - B    <0          0         0
S:
         A + B    >0         >0        <0
         A + B    <0         <0        >0
         A - B    >0         <0        <0
         A - B    <0         >0        >0

P.183, Figure 4.6, logical, in the and immediate and or immediate
|     and immediate  and $1, $2, 100 ...
|     or immediate   or  $1, $2, 100
S:
      and immediate  andi $1, $2, 100 ...
      or immediate   ori  $1, $2, 100

P.209, Figure 4.30, iteration 2, step 2
|     2: shift right Product 1111 1011 0
S:
      2: shift right Product 0000 1011 0

P.216, Figure 4.33, quotient in iteration 1, step 2b 
| iteration step    Quotient ...
|    1       2b:..   0011
S:
     1       2b:..   0000

P.220, Figure 4.37, Remainder is shifted twice in the loop (in step
|      1 and 3).  
S:
       Shifts to the left of remainder register in step 3a and 3b
       should be removed.

P.224, Figure 4.40, / sign missing
|  divide            div $2, $3    Lo = $2 $3, Hi = $2 mod $3
|  divide unsigned   divu $2, $3   Lo = $2 $3, Hi = $2 mod $3
S:
   divide            div $2, $3    Lo = $2/$3, Hi = $2 mod $3
   divide unsigned   divu $2, $3   Lo = $2/$3, Hi = $2 mod $3

P.226, in the bit pattern for float, biit -> bit
|   s       exponent           significand
|  1 biit   8 bits              23 bits
S:
    s       exponent           significand
   1 bit    8 bits              23 bits

P.243, second paragraph after The Big Picture, infinity symbol missing
|  (toward +) ... (toward -)..
S:
   (toward +infinity) ... (toward -infinity)..

P.241, Figure 4.44, Conditional branch, c.gt.s, c.ge.s etc are not part
of MIPS instructions
| FP compare single (eq, ne, lt, le, gt, ge)
| FP compare double (eq, ne, lt, le, gt, ge)
S:
  FP compare single (eq, ne, lt, le)
  FP compare double (eq, ne, lt, le)


P.244, third line in the text, the infinity symbol missing
| ... + or -; ...
S:
 ... +infinity or -infinity; ...

P.244, the table in the middle, the last row for NaN
|   255   0   2047    0    Nan (Not A Number)
S:
    255  none zero 2047 none zero  NaN (Not A Number)

P.A-21, since the offset in 0x8000($16) is signed extended to
0xFFFF8000, lw $2, 0x8000($16) actually is loading at address 0x0FFF8000,
not what was intended 0x10008000.
|  lui $16, 0x1000       # 0x1000 means ...
|  lw  $2, 0x8000($16)   # 0x10000000 + 0x8000 = 0x10008000
S:
  lui  $26, 0x1001  
  lw   $2, 0x8000($16)   # 0x10010000 + 0xFFFF8000 = 0x10008000 

P.A-48, Table
| Format 
|..
| symbol imm 
| symbol imm (register)
S:
| symbol +/- imm 
  symbol +/- imm (register)
  
P.A-62, jr bit fields and name Rsrc
|  Jr Rs     0   Rs       0     8   Jump register
|            6   5        16    5     
|  Unconditionally jump to .... register Rsrc.
S:
   Jr Rs     0   Rs       0     8   Jump register
             6   5        15    6     
   Unconditionally jump to .... register Rs.

P.E-22, E-23, Figure E.10 and E11 are identical.
|
S:

P. last, back cover, MIPS assembly language table
|  and immediate  and $1, $2, $3     $1 = $2 & $3
|  or immediate   or  $1, $2, $3     $1 = $2 | $3
S:
   and immediate  andi $1, $2, $3     $1 = $2 & $3
   or immediate   ori  $1, $2, $3     $1 = $2 | $3

